sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant CR as Scheduler/Cron
    participant J as SummaryEmailJob
    participant PR as Preferences Repo
    participant D as Directory Repository
    participant MR as Metrics Repository
    participant US as Usage Service
    participant T as Template Renderer
    participant N as Notification Service
    participant JR as Job Repository
    participant EB as Event Bus

    Note over CR,J: Periodic summaries to managers by org/team

    CR->>J: triggerSchedules()

    %% Load schedules and targets
    J->>PR: listEnabledSummaries()
    PR-->>J: summaries[{orgId, teamId?, cadence, recipients?}]
    J->>JR: createBatchRun(status="running")
    JR-->>J: {runId}

    loop for each summary
        Note over J: Resolve recipients and time window
        alt recipients provided
            J-->>J: use recipients
        else no recipients
            J->>D: listManagerEmails(orgId, teamId?)
            D-->>J: recipients[]
        end

        J-->>J: compute window = [from,to] by cadence

        par gather metrics
            J->>MR: fetchMetrics(scope=org|team, id, from, to)
            MR-->>J: metrics{}
        and gather usage
            J->>US: fetchUsage(scope=org|team, id, from, to)
            US-->>J: usage{}
        end

        Note over J: derive KPIs, deltas, trends

        J->>T: render("summary_email", {metrics, usage, window, scope})
        T-->>J: htmlBody

        par send email
            J->>N: sendEmail(to=recipients, subject="Weekly KPI summary", body=htmlBody)
            N-->>J: {messageId, result}
        and audit
            J->>JR: appendRunLog(runId, {orgId, teamId?, count=recipients.length, result})
            JR-->>J: ok
        end

        J->>EB: publish(event="summary.email.sent", payload={orgId, teamId?, window})
    end

    J->>JR: finalizeRun(runId, status="succeeded")
    JR-->>J: ok
